      "id": "2609.01836",
      "name": "EAL",
      "title": "Agent Memory Is a Surface for Endogenous Authorization Laundering",
      "version": "v1",
      "kind": "paper",
      "read_level": "METHOD_SECTIONS_READ",
      "read_sections": [
        "3.1 problem formulation; memory construction; mitigation mechanism",
        "4.6 limitations",
        "C.2 bounded event-sourcing mechanism; C.3 deployment boundaries"
      ],
      "summary_zh": "EAL 将记忆中错误权限的形成与执行器对错误权限的传播分开。其有界事件溯源让模型只抽取变更，由外部不可变日志和确定性 reducer 构造当前状态；它仍依赖正确抽取、目标绑定与已知授权主体。",
      "applicable_zh": "方法启发适用：EDM 稀疏继承须保留撤销、范围和有效期变更的可追溯关系；CEP 正文优先须保留真实证据，不能用记忆摘要自我授权。",
      "not_applicable_zh": "不能据论文证明 EDM 或 CEP 已安全：论文不覆盖实际检索、缓存失效、并发、外部执行与运行恢复。事件抽取错误也不会被 reducer 自动修正。",
      "summary_scope": "Method fit statements are inference from the stated EDM sparse-inheritance / CEP body-priority concept only, not implementation verification or performance/safety acceptance.",
